# One place pins the release toolchain.
#
# goreleaser-action reads this file via `version-file:`, tests/release-dryrun.sh
# reads both entries to choose its container images, and mise/asdf install the
# same versions locally. Before this, the goreleaser version was a quoted string
# in release.yml that the rehearsal parsed back out with sed, and git-cliff was
# pinned nowhere at all — the rehearsal ran `:latest`.
#
# That matters more than it looks once #30 lands: git-cliff decides the VERSION
# NUMBER, not just the prose. Which git-cliff runs is then part of the release,
# and `:latest` silently changing it is not something a review would catch.
goreleaser 2.17.1
git-cliff 2.13.1
